 "text": "Hi, how you've been. Basics first, a good band of armbands with an eyelet, a water bottle with a long cord, new shoes if they' blazing them. Mornings before the world wakes up are perfect for building momentum. Winter evenings are nice way to unwind. A basic runner watch without a built-in phone battery is great for basic timekeeping. A watch with heart rate monitoring is worth it for runners with breathing problems. Socks are the one where you can go wrong badly, so stick to well reviewed brands. A small bag of chocolate to reward yourself after a tough hill also helps.",
